{
  "scope": "Locked radius-four wall. Moment recovery from two fixed guarded paired fields, before comparison to signed work from separate sloping-wall displacements. All forces here are paired drive minus rest. Sources are the supported/discrete axial coordinate defects, not measured microscopic tractions.",
  "quadrature": "Q1 Gauss 2 on field elements in the meridional strip, including polar integration. Solid uses shared TerminalQuadrature(64), and the factorized vortex uses its explicit bank energy. A single native sheet/receiver cap trace is shared above the sealed slit.",
  "method": "For each cell project the angle-integrated Piola axial momentum row to RT0 face currents. Minimize the volume-weighted squared error of the mapped radial and axial moments with shared normals, subject to one divergence balance per cell and zero radial flux on the symmetry axis. The source at each internal node is minus the assembled axial configurational work divided by its lumped volume. The first closure sets its density to zero on free-boundary nodes; the second extrapolates adjacent interior-node densities; the third uses that same source and weights the axial least-squares misfit fourfold. These are recovery choices. The native solve does not independently supply the axial constraint traction or its split from sources at the held endpoints.",
  "readout": "Bank trace integrates face currents against the identical depth hat for both radial extensions. Target is the independently archived total native work including any interior extension work. Fully recovered smooth enclosure plus slit satisfies its integrated source by construction. The archived outer flux plus reconstructed slit leaves the archived outer readout unchanged and is also reported.",
